## Context

An automated digital letter generation system built for HMTI (Industrial Engineering Student Association) to streamline the preparation of official organizational correspondence through structured web forms.

## Problem

Student organization secretaries and leaders repeatedly edited Word templates by hand for borrowing, request, and invitation letters, which caused inconsistent letterheads, margin shifts, and slow turnaround times.

## My role

Owner: I mapped the three most frequent HMTI letter workflows, designed the database (`hmti_system.sql`) and role-specific dashboards, built the PHP web forms and Python document-generation scripts, and deployed the live demo.

## As-is analysis

Reviewing HMTI secretarial workflows showed that three standardized letter formats accounted for most recurring administrative requests: Surat Peminjaman (borrowing), Surat Permohonan (formal requests), and Surat Undangan (invitations), reviewed across Kahim (Chair) and Sekhim (Secretary) roles.

## Requirements

- Role-specific entry views for organization leadership (`homepage-kahim.html`) and secretariat (`homepage-sekhim.html`).
- Guided digital forms for Surat Peminjaman, Surat Permohonan, and Surat Undangan.
- Automated rendering onto official HMTI letterhead templates (`bg-surat-peminjaman.png`, `bg-surat-permohonan.png`, `bg-surat-undangan.png`).
- Structured record storage in MySQL (`hmti_system.sql`).

## Solution design

The system pairs simple PHP input forms (`form-surat-peminjaman.php`, `form-surat-permohonan.php`, `form-surat-undangan.php`) with dedicated Python document generators (`generate_peminjaman.py`, `generate_permohonan.py`, `generate_undangan.py`) so layout formatting stays locked to official templates regardless of who fills out the form.

## Build

Built with PHP, Python, MySQL, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and Docker, deployed at `generate-surat-demo.onrender.com`. Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Generate-Surat](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Generate-Surat).

## Verification

Verified form submission and automated document generation across all three letter types in the containerized Render demo.

## Outcome

Delivered a working form-based letter generator that standardizes official HMTI correspondence and eliminates manual template formatting.

## Reflection

Separating form input validation (PHP) from template rendering (Python) made it straightforward to enforce consistent official layouts without requiring officers to know document formatting tools.
